# A bf16x2 pack and an integer-to-float conversion change the value's
# bits: two stores' addresses are unknown, each with its reason. A
# cvt.u32.u64 of %tid.x + 2^32 (64 threads, from .reqntid) converts its
# low 32 bits (PTX ISA §9.7.9.22), %tid.x: the third store is at
# 4·%tid.x + param_0. A cvt.sat.u32.s32 of a parameter saturates, a
# value every thread shares, which the address keeps as one unknown term.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/cvt_reads.ptx | FileCheck --check-prefix=ANN "%s"
ANN: {{^}}	st.global.u32 	[%rd3], %r1; // global store addr ? (`cvt.rn.bf16x2.f32` is not an integer conversion){{$}}
ANN: {{^}}	st.global.u32 	[%rd5], %r1; // global store addr ? (`cvt.rn.f32.u32` is not an integer conversion){{$}}
ANN: {{^}}	st.global.u32 	[%rd9], %r1; // global store [4·%tid.x + param_0] sectors/req 4 (ideal 4){{$}}
ANN: {{^}}	st.global.u32 	[%rd11], %r1; // global store [4·uniform(%r7@{{[0-9]+}}) + param_0] sectors/req 1 (ideal 1){{$}}
